    {
      "id": "cf5ffaf3-dd7b-4196-864c-c2ebdca2189e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        176,
        -192
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 656,
        "height": 912,
        "content": "## AI Payment Note Reminder\n\n### How it works\n\n1. When a new file is added to the watched Google Drive folder, the workflow downloads it.\n2. Mistral AI runs OCR on the image, then a Groq LLM chain extracts the document date, total amount, and company name.\n3. The fields are formatted and saved to a Google Sheet (matched on the Drive file ID, so re-runs update instead of duplicating).\n4. Separately, on a daily schedule, the workflow reads the whole sheet and keeps only rows whose document date is 7, 3, 1, or 0 days away.\n5. It emails a reminder for each of those rows.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Duplicate the template [Note Sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1R3u5xaN4FCdjRRED88ZGuXBCLfi2xhSSaCHgIXtLIyw/edit?gid=0#gid=0) (File → Make a copy), keeping the same column headers.\n- [ ] Point both Google Sheets nodes to your copied sheet.\n- [ ] Set the Google Drive trigger's watched folder to your own.\n- [ ] Replace the `[ReceiverEmail]` placeholder in Send Reminder Email.\n- [ ] Configure Google Drive credentials and set up the Google Drive trigger for new files.\n- [ ] Set up Mistral AI credentials and configure the Extract Text from Image node.\n- [ ] Configure the language model chain with necessary prompts and connection settings.\n- [ ] Provide Google Sheets credentials and set up access to the notes sheet for reading and writing data.\n- [ ] Set up Gmail credentials for sending reminder messages.\n- [ ] Configure the schedule trigger for daily checking of reminders.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can customize the AI extraction and language model prompts to better suit the specific format of your documents. Adjust the filter criteria for reminder days and email content to tailor notification messages."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
