    {
      "id": "90b89296-a468-4f96-93b5-78a90cebf381",
      "name": "Parse Note Components",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1584,
        -16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are an **Information Extraction Agent**.\n\nYour task is to extract the following information from the OCR text of a document:\n\n1. `document_date`\n2. `total_amount`\n3. `company_name`\n\n### 1. DOCUMENT DATE\n\nFind the document/transaction date anywhere in the text.\n\nDates may appear in various formats, including but not limited to:\n\n* `Kendari, 12/6 2022`\n* `12/6/2022`\n* `12/06/2022`\n* `12-06-2022`\n* `12.06.2022`\n* `12 06 2022`\n* `12 Juni 2022`\n* `12 June 2022`\n* `12 Jun 2022`\n* `Juni 12, 2022`\n* `June 12, 2022`\n* `2022-06-12`\n* `2022/06/12`\n* `2022-06-12 00:00:00`\n\nOCR may introduce variations or minor errors, for example:\n\n* `12/6 2022`\n* `12 / 6 / 2022`\n* `12-6-2022`\n* `12/06/22`\n* `12 6 22`\n* `12 Jn 2022`\n* `12 Junl 2022`\n\nIf the year is written with two digits, e.g. `12/06/22`, interpret it as `2022` when the document context supports it.\n\nIf a city/location name appears before the date, e.g.:\n\n`Kendari, 12/6 2022`\n\nextract only the date.\n\nNormalize ALL dates to the format:\n\n`YYYY-MM-DD`\n\nExamples:\n\n`Kendari, 12/6 2022` → `2022-06-12`\n\n`12/06/2022` → `2022-06-12`\n\n`12 Juni 2022` → `2022-06-12`\n\n`2022/06/12` → `2022-06-12`\n\nDo NOT extract dates from:\n\n* addresses\n* phone numbers\n* invoice numbers\n* document numbers\n* item/product codes\n* due dates\n* payment dates\n\nPrioritize the date that is contextually the **document issue/transaction date**.\n\nIf multiple dates are present, choose the one that is most clearly the document/transaction date.\n\nIf no reliable date is found, use `null`.\n\n### 2. TOTAL AMOUNT\n\nFind the **grand total of the transaction**.\n\nPrioritize labels such as:\n\n* `Total`\n* `Total Rp.`\n* `TOTAL`\n* `Jumlah`\n* `Grand Total`\n* `Total Harga`\n* `Total Pembayaran`\n* `Amount`\n* `Grand Total Rp`\n* `Jumlah Total`\n\nExamples:\n\n`Total Rp. 305.000` → `305000`\n\n`TOTAL: 1.250.000` → `1250000`\n\n`Grand Total Rp 2,500,000` → `2500000`\n\nNormalize the value to an integer, removing:\n\n* `Rp`\n* `IDR`\n* thousands separators (periods)\n* thousands separators (commas)\n* spaces\n\nIf the grand total is already stated in the document, **use that total and do NOT recalculate it from the line items**.\n\nIf there is no explicit total but the line items are clear and can be safely summed, the total may be calculated.\n\nIf it cannot be determined with confidence, use `null`.\n\n### 3. COMPANY NAME\n\nFind the name of the company/store/seller that issued the document.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* the name at the very top of the document\n* the name in the header\n* a name accompanied by a company/store identity\n* a name that appears together with the seller's address or contact information\n\nExample:\n\n`TK. SINAR AGUNG`\n\n→ `company_name: \"TK. SINAR AGUNG\"`\n\nDo NOT extract:\n\n* customer names\n* recipient names\n* buyer names\n* personal names\n* addresses\n* phone numbers\n\nIf multiple names are present, choose the party that **issued/sold** the goods.\n\nIf it cannot be determined with confidence, use `null`.\n\n### OCR TEXT\n\n{{ $json.pages[0].markdown }}\n\n### OUTPUT\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nUse this EXACT structure:\n\n{\n\"document_date\": null,\n\"total_amount\": null,\n\"company_name\": null\n}\n\nRules:\n\n* Do NOT add any other fields.\n* Do NOT provide any explanation.\n* Do NOT use Markdown.\n* Do NOT guess information that is not present in the document.\n* If information is missing or ambiguous, use `null`.\n* Ensure `document_date` uses the `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n* Ensure `total_amount` is an integer.",
        "batching": {},
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
